Inspect and edit native Xray modules

Usage: xrm config [OPTIONS] [SUBCOMMAND]

OPTIONS:
  -h,   --help            Show this help message 

SUBCOMMANDS:
  modules                 List all native Xray modules and their 
                          source/runtime files 
  show                    Show one source module or the generated runtime 
                          files 
  edit                    Save a module's original JSON text 
  enable                  Include a native module in runtime 
  disable                 Disable runtime output for a native module 
  statistics              Explicitly edit native modules for traffic 
                          statistics 
  env                     Edit Xray's native env module, not xrmd's process 
                          environment 
  version                 Edit the native Xray minimum/maximum version range 
  geodata                 Edit geodata resource references and update schedule 
  api                     Edit native Xray API services without automatically 
                          opening the API 
  metrics                 Edit the native Xray Metrics listener 
  log                     Edit common native log fields 
  render                  Materialize a multi-file preview 
  check                   Run Xray's complete configuration check 
  dump                    Show Xray diagnostic dump without writing it back 
  apply                   Check saved settings while stopped, or apply them to 
                          the running core 
  export                  Export generated multi-file confdir 

GLOBAL OPTIONS (before the command):
        --socket PATH     xrmd Unix domain socket 
        --json            Write machine readable output 
        --verbose         Include original diagnostics in human errors 

Examples:
  xrm config modules Home
  xrm config show Home dns
  xrm config check Home

Next: xrm config <command> --help
